body:
This PR applies the requested targeted updates in `Mars Time 5.html`: title/header rename, additional inner numeric rings for Earth/Mars/LST clocks, and a comprehensive phone-friendly responsive layout without changing calendar/sync/theme logic.

- **Title and header copy update**
  - `<title>` changed to `Calendario Tierra - Luna & Marciano`
  - `<h1>` changed to `Calendario Tierra - Luna &amp; Marciano`

- **Clock face detail rings**
  - **`drawClock` (Earth + Mars):**
    - Added inner minute number ring for every 5 minutes (`5..55`) using subtle minute color.
  - **`drawLSTClock` (Lunar):**
    - Added centilunour labels every 10 (`10..90`) at an inner ring.
    - Added millilunour labels (`0..9`) at an innermost ring.
    - Added 10 innermost millilunour tick marks.

- **Mobile responsive CSS (app-like phone layout)**
  - Appended the full requested media-query block at the end of `<style>`:
    - `@media (max-width: 640px)` for compact controls/panels/calendar typography.
    - `@media (max-width: 400px)` for tighter clock/day sizing.
  - Added:
    ```css
    canvas.clock-face{ max-width:100%; }
    ```
    to keep canvas rendering correct at reduced sizes.

- **Example of the core clock enhancement**
  ```js
  // Draw minute numbers (every 5 min) at inner ring
  ctx.font = '6px Segoe UI,sans-serif';
  ctx.fillStyle = p.min;
  [5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55].forEach(mn => {
