`app/admin-panel/lib/permissions.ts` was conflating admin-panel entity permissions with task-specific role logic. Task permissions belong in `lib/tasks/permissions.ts`; the shared admin-panel file should only govern core entities.

## Changes

- **Removed** all task references (`Task`, `TaskPermissionScope`, `TaskUserRole`, `TaskActor`, and all `canXxxTask` / `defaultTaskRoleFromEmail` / `normalizePermissionScope` exports)
- **Replaced** with admin-only permission model scoped to the five shared entities:

```ts
import type { Client, Ad, Creative, Report, Suggestion } from "./types";

export type AdminRole = "admin" | "viewer";
export type AdminActor = { email: string; role: AdminRole };

export function isAdmin(actor: AdminActor): boolean {
  return actor.role === "admin";
}

// Per-entity guards — all delegate to isAdmin()
export function canEditClient(actor: AdminActor, _client: Client): boolean { return isAdmin(actor); }
export function canViewAd(actor: AdminActor, _ad: Ad): boolean { return isAdmin(actor); }
// ... canViewCreative, canDeleteReport, canDismissSuggestion, etc.
```

All permission functions delegate to `isAdmin()` so any future change to the admin check is a single-line update.

